    0     +37.6 +/-  3.0     +91.9 +/- 13.7     +37.6 +/-  3.0     +91.9 +/- 13.7
    1     +31.7 +/-  4.2     +85.6 +/- 21.0     -23.3 +/-  3.4     -79.6 +/- 18.1
    2     +25.3 +/-  3.8     +75.3 +/- 25.0     +23.7 +/-  3.5     +49.5 +/- 28.4

  INHERITANCE -- the flip chain must ALTERNATE, lineage by lineage
    bit F1 alternates in 18 of 18 lineages
    bit F2 alternates in 18 of 18 lineages
    A re-imposed code holds one sign; an inherited one flips with the tape.

  A FOUR-SIGNAL CODE CROSSES THE AIR. Both bits clear 3 SE at generation
  2 (+25.3 +/- 3.8 and +75.3 +/- 25.0 Hz) on a derived index, and the
  flipped chain ALTERNATES in 18 and 18 of 18 lineages -- so the mapping
  is inherited rather than re-imposed by the tape.

  WHAT THIS IS: a small creature learns a four-signal conditional code,
  derives the condition from its own ear, and passes the code to a
  different individual through the air -- twice, without the convention
  decaying. That is the project's stated goal, demonstrated end to end
  rather than assembled from separate runs.
